<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-10-17T12:16:12Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>France faces day of cost-of-living protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:015205af5b267fc00c59c5619891caf50530eb5d626c98f7cb83b73ebf5e0aef</id><updated>2026-10-17T12:16:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T11:47:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261017-france-faces-day-of-cost-of-living-protests" /><summary type="html">French authorities detained dozens on Saturday at the start of nationwide protests against the cost of living, in what is likely to be a key indicator of the social climate heading toward elections to replace President Emmanuel Macron. France 24's Antonia Kerrigan tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Cameroonian journalist shot in Bamenda</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7388156118b5ee2f9828aeaf7092be2690a60452fc4bc3d118bf9056e5597269</id><updated>2026-10-17T12:16:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T11:16:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261017-cameroonian-journalist-shot-in-bamenda" /><summary type="html">Cameroonian journalist Ambe Macmillan is recovering in hospital after being shot in the legs by gunmen in the north-western city of Bamenda. A young woman was also killed as the attackers opened fire on mourners attending a wake. The shooting has renewed concerns about the dangers facing journalists in Cameroon's English-speaking regions, after years of conflict between government forces and separatist groups.</summary></entry><entry><title>Uganda launches Ebola vaccine trial</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9ffe2b61be7046a263a2cdb28aa49613489a2af5740bf61dbc297a6cd8fb76d8</id><updated>2026-10-17T12:16:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T11:00:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261017-uganda-launches-ebola-vaccine-trial" /><summary type="html">The town of Masaka in southern Uganda is currently conducting a Phase 1 trial of a vaccine candidate against the Bundibugyo strain of the Ebola virus, which is circulating in the region. There is currently no approved treatment or vaccine for this strain.</summary></entry><entry><title>Kenya reports third Ebola case, contact tracing continues</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:48e778593bb40e115dd87644c3a9184b4a595144c07056e324962d12e83c111e</id><updated>2026-10-17T12:16:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T10:56:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261017-kenya-reports-third-ebola-case-contact-tracing-continues" /><summary type="html">Kenya has confirmed a third case of Ebola, a relative of a man who died earlier this month after travelling from the Democratic Republic of the Congo. The health ministry said the 65-year-old woman tested positive while in quarantine, where she has been since 5 October. The second patient, a 39-year-old man from the same family, is in a stable condition. Health officials say there is no evidence of community transmission, as both individuals were under quarantine. However, three contacts have yet to be traced. Our correspondent Bastien Renouil tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Russia hails Trump waiving sanctions as 'historic'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:be9db540322e486e23eeaf8472606421bf514d2ea59bacc1aa861eb97d66a23a</id><updated>2026-10-17T12:16:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T10:41:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261017-russia-hails-trump-waiving-sanctions-as-historic" /><summary type="html">Russia on Saturday hailed US President Donald Trump's move to waive new sanctions on it as "historic", as Ukraine worries he is taking Moscow's side in Europe's worst conflict since World War II.</summary></entry><entry><title>Coastal homes burn as hot winds fuel California fires</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:779ddb48e1e58cc2a1a05c96b9c7c0963e7841a9bf39cc85b65a4af83e5ff4e7</id><updated>2026-10-17T12:16:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T10:37:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261017-coastal-homes-burn-as-hot-winds-fuel-california-fires" /><summary type="html">A fast-moving fire fueled by high winds burned at least six homes in Southern California on Friday, engulfing expensive coastal properties and prompting thousands to evacuate.</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump's new press secretary out after less than week</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a43a94441bdc884ef97a841877ddf62d2413f60d546c1bd3dfa5d644a7a407a1</id><updated>2026-10-17T12:16:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T10:36:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261017-trump-s-new-press-secretary-out-after-less-than-week" /><summary type="html">White House Press Secretary Katie Zacharia was pushed out Friday after less than a week in the high-profile job following a series of blunders that added to distractions for her embattled boss, President Donald Trump.</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump says did not order curb to Starshield for Ukraine</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:17eb76e52241bc74029d4fdf11d421adab39e0c9c8d7603149ce3502ca378196</id><updated>2026-10-17T12:16:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T10:19:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261017-trump-says-did-not-order-curb-to-starshield-for-ukraine" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump said Friday he did not request a reduction in Starshield services for Ukraine, after tech billionaire Elon Musk insisted any limits on the SpaceX-operated communications system would ultimately have come from the US president.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ligue 1: Paris Saint-Germain aim to build on recent progress at Strasbourg</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5c10d8b80c28440cc83804997552a403f3dc2dc5e9b4ffc48a2efcbe0cf8a527</id><updated>2026-10-17T12:16:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T09:41:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/sports/20261017-ligue-1-paris-saint-germain-aim-to-build-on-recent-progress-at-strasbourg" /><summary type="html">Fresh from their impressive 4-2 Champions League win on Manchester City’s home turf on Wednesday, PSG travel to Strasbourg on Saturday in Ligue 1. They aim to secure a fourth consecutive league win and maintain their growing momentum ahead of Tuesday's Champions League showdown with Barcelona.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Zelensky drums up European backing as Trump ties slump</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ff372e12477b2c86285afb8bb6a07710fb102da2a0533a2e4f0f39e0199c2b86</id><updated>2026-10-17T12:16:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T09:25:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261017-zelensky-drums-up-european-backing-as-trump-ties-slump" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky urged EU leaders Friday to keep financing Kyiv's fight with nearly $80 billion more next year, as he insisted he was standing up for his country amid a fresh row with US President Donald Trump.</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump waives new Russia sanctions as Ukraine ties slump</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e86337a26728e8309a408de9373f7324387c140b58e18a5a7669eed34a6093bd</id><updated>2026-10-17T12:16:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T09:23:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261017-trump-waives-new-russia-sanctions-as-ukraine-ties-slump" /><summary type="html">President Donald Trump signed an executive order on Friday that waived sweeping US sanctions and tariffs targeting Russia's energy revenues, marking a new low in Washington's ties with war-torn Ukraine. Our correspondent Gulliver Cragg tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Students, trade unions and Yellow Vests set to protest across France</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:600e0b9ba134e10af7822cd15ead5d467760a6745a59aa14e878ebf9a57e4656</id><updated>2026-10-17T12:16:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T09:11:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261017-students-trade-unions-and-yellow-vests-set-to-protest-across-france" /><summary type="html">Tens of thousands of ⁠people are expected to ​protest across France on Saturday, as students, trade unionists and remnants of the Yellow Vest movement join forces to demonstrate against high prices and ​the country's fraying social model.</summary></entry><entry><title>Yemen's Houthis claim responsibility for fresh missile strike on Aden airport</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:500e4639f37c68eb1fc1f4d17cd3745fc3f2270dbb22a321a1d3200308c09ded</id><updated>2026-10-17T12:16:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T06:00:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261017-yemen-s-houthis-claim-responsibility-for-fresh-missile-strike-on-aden-airport" /><summary type="html">Yemen's Iran-aligned Houthi group claimed responsibility after two missiles struck Aden International Airport on Friday, saying they had targeted a weapons depot as well as a military command headquarters. The Aden Security Department said a Yemenia Airways flight bound for Cairo had been preparing for takeoff when the attack took place.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Live: Police crack down as protesters try to raise barricades across France</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8b9c251de9adfafd0749450a765569f2dff1fd74b886ca4845d8cb44f02b94c6</id><updated>2026-10-17T12:16:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T05:17:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261017-live-france-s-yellow-vests-throw-their-weight-behind-mounting-student-protests" /><summary type="html">French police used tear gas and batons to try to drive protesters from the streets in Paris, Marseille and Lyon as demonstrators staged unsanctioned marches and tried to block traffic with impromptu barricades Saturday. Hundreds of thousands of people are expected to demonstrate across France as students, trade union members and remnants of the Yellow Vest movement join forces to protest rising cost of living. Follow our liveblog for the latest updates.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>Zelensky turns to Europe for backing as ties with Trump deteriorate</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8a053260404649359999b533d34d365056e565326cfbba84078ba191634f388b</id><updated>2026-10-17T12:16:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T20:25:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261016-zelensky-turns-to-europe-for-backing-as-ties-with-trump-deteriorate" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky turned to his European allies on Friday, asking Brussels for an additional €70 billion to fund the war against Russia next year. Zelensky's relationship with US President Donald Trump deteriorated after the US eased sanctions on Moscow as part of a diesel-supply deal.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>KENYA CONFIRMS THIRD EBOLA CASE</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0a63fb14c79248864aa0718b62ff5c24c6f87b14949162c4d32465d5b92120cc</id><updated>2026-10-17T12:16:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T20:25:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/kenya-confirms-third-ebola-case" /><summary type="html">In tonight's programme, Kenya confirms a third case of Ebola, a relative of a man who died earlier this month after travelling from DR Congo. Also,Cameroonian journalist Ambe Macmillan is recovering in hospital after being shot in the legs by gunmen in Bamenda. And we meet Ghanaian artist Ibrahim Mahama... And finally, we meet Ghanaian artist Ibrahim Mahama, who digs deep into his country's colonial and industrial past to lay new creative foundations for generations to come.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>'Finish what we started': After student protests, France braces for return of the Yellow Vests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3a542baf41c4263a1ea0f280b65c08e26429ca71dcb8f38066378908dce59982</id><updated>2026-10-17T12:16:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T20:10:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261016-finish-what-we-started-after-student-protests-france-braces-return-yellow-vests" /><summary type="html">An online movement against rising fuel prices has gained momentum ahead of planned nationwide demonstrations on October 17 with former Yellow Vest figures set to join the protests in support of high-school students. Some are drawing parallels between the latest action and the 2018 cost-of-living protests that rattled President Emmanuel Macron's first term in office.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Clashes grip Tirana as Albanian PM blames 'foreign hands' for mounting unrest</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8783941eb80f482a098b2379ccb4890d16aee99fa60789da1d8fd50a6e5e8edb</id><updated>2026-10-17T12:16:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T19:59:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261016-clashes-grip-tirana-as-albanian-pm-blames-foreign-hands" /><summary type="html">Albanian Prime Minister Edi Rama on Friday blamed the involvement of “foreign hands” for escalating protests, which he said are aimed at hindering Albania's bid to join the European Union. Thousands of demonstrators have taken to the streets of Albania's capital since Tuesday, demanding Rama’s resignation and denouncing university conditions and high tuition fees.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Trump Vs Zelensky, From the Screen to the Streets, Gen Z protests from Paris to Dehli</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:400a598a544049be7e3574e69620abcfdd29d3f2558377b4471ea4990e8e4809</id><updated>2026-10-17T12:16:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T19:21:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-world-this-week/20261016-trump-vs-zelensky-from-the-screen-to-the-streets-gen-z-protests-from-paris-to-dehli" /><summary type="html">In India, the Cockroach movement felt the crushing boot of the state this week. Thousands of Gen Z protesters were rounded up and detained in sports stadiums and community halls turned into makeshift detention centres, while the movement’s founder, Abhijeet Dipke, was arrested on arrival. A mass demonstration over alleged voter fraud was effectively crushed before it could begin.And Abdijeet has been detained again todayNarendra Modi’s government says the measures were necessary to protect civilians in the capital. But he now faces accusations of choosing repression over democracy, with the UN Human Rights Office urging authorities to respect the right to peaceful assembly. 
 
 
 
It’s been a week of blame games and accusations of betrayal in Ukraine with President Zelensky speaking of his personal hurt at President Trump’s decision to make a diesel deal with the Kremlin ahead of the US Mid term elections calling it “weak”, suggesting Trump had chosen, “the other side”. Trump meanwhile made clear he wants Zelensky replaced, and warned him against striking Russian refineries AND announced an energy ceasefire, declaring it to have been agreed by both sides but which went nowhere. President Zelensky continued to search for solidarity and a solution in Europe.
 
 
 
