Gavin Lee is joined this week by Anne-Elisabeth Moutet, John Sweeney, Victor Mallet and Suhasini Raj.</summary><category term="The World This Week" /></entry><entry><title>'US tilting toward Russia: Europeans are standing more and more solidly with Zelensky'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ac28eba5dc33e48ffa44c5cc22645f603fea3ec697515946b79d8627f5dfe977</id><updated>2026-10-17T12:16:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T18:33:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261016-us-tilting-toward-russia-europeans-are-standing-more-and-more-solidly-with-zelensky" /><summary type="html">As transatlantic relations confront renewed geopolitical uncertainty, former Estonian President Toomas Hendrik Ilves delivers a pointed assessment of Washington's shifting approach to Russia's war on Ukraine and the profound implications for European security. At the heart of his analysis lies a fundamental question: can Europe develop the political unity, strategic independence and military capabilities necessary to defend its interests in an increasingly unpredictable international order?  Ilves response: "If there's any time for Europe to begin to act as Europe and not as being strictly self-interested, then this is the time for it."</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Sally Rooney's books no longer sold in UK over support for banned pro-Palestinian group</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:478eb5e60fd9629a595fc9265fa9b0dd3fcfbe5991ffbb2ca059afbea5cc88cd</id><updated>2026-10-17T12:16:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T16:26:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261016-sally-rooney-s-books-no-longer-sold-in-uk-over-support-for-banned-pro-palestinian-group" /><summary type="html">Irish novelist Sally ⁠Rooney's books will ​no longer be sold in Britain over her plans to use her royalties ​to support Palestine Action, a pro-Palestinian group banned as a terrorist organisation, Rooney and her publisher said on Wednesday. The bestselling author, known for novels including "Normal People" and "Conversations with ​Friends", has ‌been a vocal supporter of Palestine Action, including after ⁠it was proscribed by the British government under terrorism laws last year.</summary></entry><entry><title>Argentine demonstration over education cuts ends in clashes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fd7d6a9de20dd5414150ebfe5ea32d2f06aa2eb5238f66c40194729a0d0e3b87</id><updated>2026-10-17T12:16:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T16:25:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261016-argentine-demonstration-over-education-cuts-ends-in-clashes" /><summary type="html">Argentine demonstrators clashed with police on Thursday at a major protest in Buenos Aires over budget-slashing President Javier Milei's higher education spending. The main demonstration outside parliament by thousands of university students and staff, trade unionists and opposition activists remained peaceful. But dozens of mostly hooded demonstrators who broke away from the crowd lobbed stones and other projectiles at the police, who responded with tear gas and water cannons.</summary></entry><entry><title>Embattled new White House Press Secretary Zacharia 'let go' from her role</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a48ff069ff9ae4bf0c968876e95f45e66f65bca39d67caf027d1a94ce1fbb354</id><updated>2026-10-17T12:16:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T15:57:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261016-embattled-new-white-house-press-secretary-zacharia-let-go-from-her-role" /><summary type="html">A White House Press official said Friday that Secretary ​Katie Zacharia was "let go" from her role after US President Donald Trump signaled she was on her way out, a week after he picked her for the post. Zacharia's credentials as an attorney had come under scrutiny and she admitted to not having passed the bar in an interview with Fox News on Thursday.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>'Finish what we started': After student protests, France braces for return of the Yellow Vests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9e629a5bc5c1b2d2b1756b19c5f376091781662df880a74b1f18bbec1270147d</id><updated>2026-10-17T12:16:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T15:55:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261016-cost-of-living-demonstrations-to-grip-pre-election-france" /><summary type="html">An online movement against rising fuel prices has gained momentum ahead of planned nationwide demonstrations on October 17 with former Yellow Vest figures set to join the protests in support of high-school students. Some are drawing parallels between the latest action and the 2018 cost-of-living protests that rattled President Emmanuel Macron's first term in office.</summary></entry></feed>
